    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Special letters",
     "texto": [
      "The Turkish alphabet has **29 letters**. Its seven special letters are **ç, ğ, ı, İ, ö, ş, ü**.",
      "The **ı** has no dot and sounds like a central vowel; the **i** does have a dot. In capitals, **i → İ** and **ı → I**.",
      "**ç** sounds like «ch», **ş** sounds like «sh», **ö** and **ü** are similar to the German vowels, and **ğ** usually lengthens the vowel before it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
